!deck: Math Identities
!tags: Math Trigonometric Hyperbolic Identity
!type: Cloze Math

!id: zvAyOSCTQW
!text:
\[
{{c2::e^{ix}::\ldots}}
=
{{c1::\cos x + i \sin x::\ldots}}
\]

Euler's Formula
~~~

!id: Rjr9k6j6ba
!text:
\[
{{c2::e^{-ix}::\ldots}}
=
{{c1::\cos x - i \sin x::\ldots}}
\]

Euler's Formula
~~~

!id: inJ6BD8ofs
!text:
\[
{{c2::\left( \cos(x) + i \sin(x) \right)^n::\ldots}}
=
{{c1::\cos(nx) + i \sin(nx)::\ldots}}
\]

De Moivre's Formula
!back extra:
For \( x \in \mathbb{R} \) and \( n \in \mathbb{Z} \), Euler's formula and the exponential power law give
\[
\begin{align*}
(\cos x + i\sin x)^n
&= (e^{ix})^n \\
&= e^{inx} \\
&= \cos(nx) + i\sin(nx).
\end{align*}
\]
~~~

!id: kBXzrvvubz
!text:
\[
{{c2::z^n = 1::\ldots}}
\iff
{{c1::z = e^{2\pi i k / n}, \quad k = 0, 1, \ldots, n-1::\ldots}}
\]

\( n \)th Roots of Unity
!back extra:
- Write \( z = re^{i\theta} \), so \( z^n = r^n e^{in\theta} \).
- Note that \( 1 = e^{i \cdot 2\pi k} \) for any integer \( k \).
- Matching moduli and arguments forces \( r = 1 \) and \( n\theta = 2\pi k \), i.e. \( \theta = 2\pi k / n \).
- Taking \( k = 0, 1, \ldots, n-1 \) gives all \( n \) distinct roots; larger \( k \) only repeats these by the \( 2\pi \)-periodicity of \( e^{i\theta} \).
~~~

!id: HyyVM3fcRE
!text:
For \( r > 0 \) and \( \theta \in \mathbb{R} \), the **complex logarithm** (all values) is given by

\[
{{c2::\ln(re^{i\theta})::\ldots}}
=
{{c1::\left\{ \ln r + i(\theta + 2\pi k) : k \in \mathbb{Z} \right\}::\ldots}}
\]

When \( -\pi < \theta \le \pi \) the **principal value** is

\[
{{c4::\operatorname{Log}(re^{i\theta})::\ldots}}
=
{{c3::\ln r + i\theta::\ldots}}
\]
!back extra:
\[
\begin{align*}
e^{\ln r + i(\theta + 2\pi k)}
&= e^{\ln r}e^{i\theta}e^{2\pi ik} \\
&= re^{i\theta}(\cos(2\pi k) + i \cdot \sin(2\pi k)) \\
&= re^{i\theta}(1 + i \cdot 0) \\
&= re^{i\theta}
\end{align*}
\]
~~~
